@title Autumn Grants Round: Funding Order Worksheet
@subtitle $400,000 to give out, 14 requests, staff order by score as the starting point
@width wide

! This page is a fixed worksheet, not a live tool: it cannot be dragged or recalculated. It gives the staff order, the running total against $400,000, where the money runs out, every condition that must be settled first, and a decision sheet to fill in and send to the grants clerk.

kpi Available | $400,000
kpi Requested | $773,850 | 1.9 times the money | bad
kpi Short by | $373,850 | requests over budget | bad
kpi Conditional requests | $359,400 | 5 of 14 requests | bad

# Staff order, with the running total

Staff order is by score, highest first. The running total adds each request in full, in that order, against the $400,000.

data run = ref,running total; G-102,62500; G-111,103500; G-106,158300; G-101,206300; G-110,228450; G-105,315750; G-112,410750; G-109,487150; G-114,537150; G-103,572350; G-108,602250; G-113,635850; G-104,755850; G-107,773850

chart bar run y=running total target="400000 budget" unit=$ title="Running total of requests in staff order"

!! In staff order the money runs out at **G-112** (Calloway Valley Fire Safe Council). After the first six requests, $315,750 is committed and $84,250 is left, but G-112 asks for $95,000: **$10,750 more than what remains**. The panel must either fund G-112 partly, defer it, or skip to a smaller request.

