# Rules a choice can break

Five requests are conditional. Whatever order the panel agrees, committing money to any of these before its condition is settled breaks a rule.

table = ref,applicant,requested,condition to settle first; G-104,Third Ward Neighborhood Council,"$120,000","Find out what the city will fund, since it may fund part of this."; G-107,Marisol Vega (individual),"$18,000","Not a registered charity, so a fiscal sponsor is needed."; G-109,The Brightwater Theatre,"$76,400","Written consent from the building owner has not been given."; G-112,Calloway Valley Fire Safe Council,"$95,000","Decide whether it conflicts with G-104, which is in the same neighborhood."; G-114,Unity Credit Circle,"$50,000","Seeking match funding, and none is confirmed yet."

!! G-112 is both the request that crosses the $400,000 line in staff order and a conditional one. G-104 and G-112 together ask for $215,000, more than half the budget.

# Other things the panel will weigh

- **G-101** ($48,000, score 86): two panelists want a smaller ask, so this is a likely partial grant.
- **G-105** ($87,300, score 83): vehicles are 70% of the cost, about $61,100.
- **G-113** ($33,600, score 72): stipends are $11,200 of the request, a third of it.
- **G-103** ($35,200, score 78): a new applicant, so no track record with the foundation.
- **G-111** ($41,000, score 90): urgent, because the current freezer is failing.

# One alternative to compare

If the panel funds in staff order but holds back all five conditional requests (G-104, G-107, G-109, G-112, G-114), the funded set is G-102, G-111, G-106, G-101, G-110, G-105, G-103 and G-108. That commits $380,850 and leaves $19,150. The next request in line, G-113 at $33,600, would be $14,450 over, so it would need a partial grant or a deferral.

# Decision sheet for the grants clerk

Fill in one line per request. Decision is one of: Funded in full, Funded partly (type the amount), Deferred, Declined. Add the reason for any change from the staff order.

